# Scenario video-assert-mismatch (plan 06-13, V6-10, T-06-18): outcome guest-fail, exit 10. The
# Foreground/Background run of the third diagnostic with one deliberately wrong frame hash (the first
# digit of the sha256-text of F-D1 changed), so the one failing clause is the frame hash assert and a
# vacuous video assert cannot pass.
# expect-detail: assert=24 line=37 frame 0 hash == 96b80eb73c51152ac252a1bbebcc86ead4535ac9ebdbf2a346bd8bf1b0383596 got 86b80eb73c51152ac252a1bbebcc86ead4535ac9ebdbf2a346bd8bf1b0383596
ivss 1
id video-assert-mismatch
profile intv-2609-ntsc-family-p1
content exec boot-stub
content grom zero-grom
content cart diag-stic-1.ivsc
capture video 0 1
run-to 150000 ticks stop halted
assert halted == yes
assert mem 02F0 == 03C5
assert mem 02F1 == 00FF
assert mem 02A3 == 2A01
assert mem 02A4 == 0E0A
assert mem 02A5 == 1A13
assert mem 02A6 == 381C
assert mem 02DC == 2C1D
assert mem 02EF == 1C0F
assert mem 0200 == 0000
assert frame 0 displayed == yes
assert frame 0 pixel 0 0 == 0
assert frame 0 pixel 158 0 == 0
assert frame 0 pixel 24 64 == 1
assert frame 0 pixel 24 65 == 5
assert frame 0 pixel 33 65 == 3
assert frame 0 pixel 41 65 == 3
assert frame 0 pixel 49 64 == 12
assert frame 0 pixel 0 88 == 5
assert frame 0 pixel 1 88 == 6
assert frame 0 pixel 152 88 == 7
assert frame 0 pixel 158 95 == 7
assert frame 0 pixel 153 89 == 10
assert frame 0 hash == 96b80eb73c51152ac252a1bbebcc86ead4535ac9ebdbf2a346bd8bf1b0383596
assert video count == 1
